B.1.1. {"problem": "The declaration changed: a new Element property and a new propose_element param were added. The header still gives authoring as 'interface 1, domain version 9'. The version and the interface/handoff statements ('interface 1.x') were not updated. The EXAMPLES.md scenarios do not cover drafted_by either, so the new behaviour has no worked example.", "where": "SKILL.md header (authoring domain version 9, interface 1); EXAMPLES.md Authoring scenarios", "kind": "reference"}
B.2.0. {"problem": "The change aims to show which agent drafted badly, but propose_element is an owner-only action, so actor.id is the owner and never the agent. drafted_by is an optional free-text param that the owner types in. It can be left out, mistyped, or name the wrong agent. Elements proposed without it carry no attribution, and nothing checks the value against any agent. The owner therefore cannot rely on it to tell which agent drafted badly.", "where": "SKILL.md, propose_element (drafted_by param and effect) and the Element.drafted_by property", "kind": "behaviour"}
B.2.1. {"problem": "The effect 'sets target.drafted_by to params.drafted_by' is unconditional, but the param is optional. The spec does not say what happens when it is omitted. Other optional-param effects in the document, such as request_delivery's replaced_commit, state the 'if present, otherwise unset' case. This effect leaves it open whether drafted_by stays unset or is set to an empty or undefined value.", "where": "SKILL.md, propose_element effect", "kind": "other"}
B.3.0. {"problem": "The change says it records which agent drafted each proposed element, but propose_element is an owner-only action. drafted_by is an optional free-text param the owner types in, not taken from the drafting agent's identity (nothing like actor.id is recorded for the agent). When the owner omits or misreports it, the element carries no agent or the wrong one. Because the param is optional, the 'each proposed element' goal is not met and the owner cannot reliably tell which agent drafted badly.", "where": "SKILL.md, propose_element (drafted_by param and effect) and the Element.drafted_by property", "kind": "behaviour"}
