B.4.0. {"problem": "The request is to record which agent drafted each proposed element, but drafted_by is optional both as a property and as a propose_element param. An owner who omits it leaves the element with no drafter, and the owner then cannot tell which agent drafted badly. No precondition or invariant requires it, unlike the existing invariant `elements-cite-a-source`, which does enforce citing a source.", "where": "SKILL.md, propose_element params and the Element.drafted_by property", "kind": "behaviour"}
B.4.1. {"problem": "propose_element is an owner-only action, so the agent that did the drafting never takes it. drafted_by is therefore a free-text string typed by the owner, not the acting agent's identity, and nothing checks it. Unlike first_confirmer, which is set from actor.id, it can be wrong or made up, which weakens its use for finding the agent that drafted badly. The Element object description and the glossary still say elements are 'proposed/drafted by an agent', which does not match who takes the action.", "where": "SKILL.md, propose_element effect; Element object description and glossary 'element'", "kind": "other"}
